# Stoicism
Stoicism — Things You Should Never Do. Wisdom from the ancients on what to avoid.
1. Don't Suffer Imagined Troubles – Seneca. Worry doesn't prevent pain — it multiplies it. Face what comes when it comes.
2. Don't Tie Your Identity To Things You Own – Seneca. Your worth is not in possessions. They come and go. You remain.
3. Don't Be Overheard Complaining — Not Even To Yourself – Marcus Aurelius. Complaining gives power to what you can't control. Silence rebuilds it.
4. You Mess Up Too, So Don't Judge Other People – Marcus Aurelius. We're all flawed. Be kind.
5. Don't Compare Yourself To Others – Epictetus. Your path is yours alone. Comparison steals joy.
6. Don't Talk More Than You Listen – Zeno. Two ears, one mouth. Listen twice as much as you speak.



