# Enneagram three instinctual subtypes
The three instinctual subtypes in the Enneagram show which life area a person channels their energy into.
Everyone has all three, but one is dominant, one secondary, and one weakest (the blind spot).
The ordering colors how each type shows up.
SP (Self-preservation): Focuses on survival and comfort: health, food, home, money, safety, energy, and routines.
SX (Sexual / one-to-one): Focuses on intensity, attraction, and one-to-one bonds: passionate relationships, chemistry, deep connection, competition, and possessiveness.
SO (Social): Focuses on groups and community: belonging, status, friend circles, social roles, and the question “where do I stand in this group?”


